{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Within your gates you shall eat it.</b> Some say the priest eats it outside the Temple, and some say: once it has a blemish, it is permitted to an Israelite. This is far-fetched in my eyes." "<b>The impure and the pure.</b> Return, you shall eat it. And the meaning is like the phrase 'whether you are impure or pure,' and the meaning is: whether one is impure or pure, it is permitted to eat it, because the flesh of consecrated offerings, if an impure person ate it, is subject to karet. And because it mentioned 'year,' it mentioned it three times, and further, on account of the firstborn, which is eaten in the Temple, and likewise the Paschal offering is eaten in the Temple and not outside it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {1 "Reading 'שב אתה תאכלנו' as 'Return, you shall eat it,' referring back to the preceding verb; the Hebrew is elliptical and possibly corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:37.476211777Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}